  "content": {
    "body": "A **memory** pebble is a durable FACT store distilled from chat sessions —\nwhat was learned or decided that should PERSIST across sessions, so agents\ndon't relearn it. It answers \"what we already KNOW / decided\". Memory is\nWRITTEN from a session (the chat's Save-to-Memory action, or the AI's\nremember step) and READ by agents as durable context at the start of a\nrun.\n\nMemory vs knowledge: **knowledge** is an authored, curated DOCUMENT about\nthe system; **memory** is a captured, session-scoped set of FACTS from\nactual work. Knowledge is written on purpose; memory accretes from doing.\n\n## Pebble-level components\n\n- **name** — the memory's topic (\"RentSpree webhook quirks\").\n- **status** — AI-side lifecycle: Draft (`planned`) → Active (`verified`) →\n  Inactive (`deprecated`); most memories are simply Active.\n- **description** — one-line recall hook.\n- **references** — memory may reference the pebbles its facts are about\n  (a model, a workflow, an api).\n- **resources** — a memory MAY link code when a fact is about a specific\n  file (via `link-code`); often it just carries the facts.\n\n## Content components — the categories under a memory\n\n- **context** — where this memory came from: the agent / session / date.\n- **summary** — a short digest of what happened or what was learned.\n- **facts** — the distilled durable facts, ONE per entry. This is the part\n  agents LOAD — keep each fact atomic, true, and self-contained.\n- **transcript** — optional raw conversation transcript (markdown), kept\n  for provenance; agents read the facts, not this.\n\n## Quick map — component → what's under it\n\n| Component | Under it |\n|---|---|\n| pebble.name | memory topic (string) |\n| pebble.status | Draft (planned) · Active (verified) · Inactive (deprecated) |\n| pebble.description | one-line recall hook |\n| references | pebbles the facts are about |\n| resources | code links (optional) |\n| content.context | origin — agent / session / date |\n| content.summary | short digest |\n| content.facts | atomic durable facts (the part agents load) |\n| content.transcript | optional raw conversation |\n\n## Memory CLI — all memory operations live here\n\nContent kind is **memory**. Usually a memory is produced by the chat's\nSave-to-Memory action; the CLI creates one directly too. `content` is\nwritten WHOLE.\n\nCREATE:\n\n    pebbles-cli create memory --title \"RentSpree webhook quirks\" --content '{\n      \"kind\": \"memory\",\n      \"context\": \"From the SR-import investigation, 2026-07\",\n      \"summary\": \"How RentSpree webhooks behave and where they are handled\",\n      \"facts\": [\n        { \"text\": \"RentSpree retries a failed webhook up to 5x with backoff\" },\n        { \"text\": \"Idempotency key is the external application id\" }\n      ],\n      \"transcript\": \"\"\n    }'\n\nSTATUS / references / inspect / retire:\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status memory/rentspree-webhook-quirks.pebble verified\n    pebbles-cli refs memory/rentspree-webhook-quirks.pebble\n    pebbles-cli get memory/rentspree-webhook-quirks.pebble\n    pebbles-cli set-status memory/rentspree-webhook-quirks.pebble deprecated\n\n## Related\n\nDurable facts complement authored **knowledge**; both are loaded as\ncontext, but memory is captured from sessions while knowledge is written.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-27T17:07:12.820Z",
  "description": "The component CATALOG of a Memory pebble (durable FACTS distilled from chat sessions — what was learned that must persist across sessions): its content components (context, summary, facts, transcript), how it is produced (from a chat session) and consumed (agents load its facts), and the full memory pebbles-cli usage. A DEFINITION reference skills point at.",
